From cd1295edba0e73a4966d858100b8b1fde96033d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NovaFemme <noreply@example.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:36:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add Halo: a decorative burst-ring view

A radial ring of spectrum-driven streaks with bubbles drifting through it.
Display only - each streak is auto-gained against its own recent range, so it
is deliberately not a meter.

- web/renderers/halo.js, registered as the 13th view
- theme roles halo.bg / halo.core / halo.bubble.a-d, mode.halo, and a
  'halo' ramp in nova-dark and nova-ice
- strokes batched by colour/alpha bucket (~130 per frame, not ~600+bubbles)
- dev/tests/halotest.mjs (node-canvas, no Playwright): 11 checks
- doccheck: README table match was anchored to a header shape the table no
  longer had, so it had been failing; now anchored to the section heading

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VW5MFeLib8XK71BWatHSd4
